WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:06.900
Ask an AI about your own docs, and it invents an answer —
it never saw your data.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:14.000
A model only knows what it was trained on: frozen, months old,
and public — not your private, current data.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:30.900
RAG fixes that. First you index your docs — split them into chunks,
embed them as vectors, store them. Then, to answer a question,
you retrieve the closest passages and hand them to the model as context.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:40.200
It doesn't memorize your data — it looks it up, fresh every time,
and cites the source.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:46.700
That's RAG. Learn to build it at Sage Academy — or have it built for you.
